# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PERSONAL HEALTH DATA — these stay local. Do not remove these lines.
#
# The *.example.md templates are the committed versions: they carry the
# structure and the generic, non-personal norms without any dated records.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Live memory files (accumulated personal norms and sleep signatures)
skills/health-episode-report/HealthMonitoringNorms.md
skills/scored-sleep-signature/SleepSignatureLog.md

# The PII denylist used by tools/check-public-safe.sh. A list of someone's
# medications and symptoms IS the personal data — never commit it. The
# committed artifact is tools/.pii-terms.example.
tools/.pii-terms

# Dated norms versions pulled down from the Minowa document store
**/HealthMonitoringNorms_*.md
**/SleepSignatureLog_*.md

# Generated reports and intake output — these contain HR, medications,
# symptoms and observations. Matches dated filenames only, so
# assets/report_template.html is unaffected.
20??-??-??_*.html
20??-??-??_*.md
outputs/
reports/
intake/

# Raw exports from Minowa / Garmin
*.minowa.json
garmin_export*
*.csv

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.venv/
